set-bg: img/map_2.jpg
new-page: true

> *"Bourgeois society stands at the crossroads, either transition to socialism or regression into barbarism."*

 - Rosa Luxemburg, *The Junius Pamphlet*, 1916

This is a game of alternate history. While historical accuracy is a major concern, keep in mind that this is a *game*, and that any divergence from actual events will necessarily have to involve some element of make-believe. It takes the side of the working class, and for that reason it does not flatter the party you lead: the KPD will make mistakes, some of them of its own making and some imposed from Moscow, and the game will say so. Nothing here is random: if your decisions are right, the outcome follows.

It is January 1923. The Central Committee has met, and it has chosen you to lead the Communist Party of Germany (KPD). Moscow has sent its congratulations, the factions have sent their demands, and the workers of the Ruhr and of Saxony are waiting to see what kind of leader you will be. The party is yours now, with all that it has inherited.

- @1923_easy: Begin (easy difficulty)
- @1923_main: Begin (medium difficulty)
- @1923_hard: Begin (hard difficulty)
- @1923_historical: Begin (historical mode)

